jess: healthcheck note — NLB wants TCP health checks by default. if you have externalTrafficPolicy: Local your readiness probe must be reachable on the node IP the NLB targets. if the pod binds hostNetwork or you use hostPort it's different. TL;DR: use tcpSocket readiness or make sure nodePort is open and pod readiness uses same port. we hit 503s last time because probes were http on 8080 but NLB was probing nodeport on 31000 -> mismatch.

sam: quick terraform snippet that worked for us with AWS NLB + gateway (for reference):
```
resource "kubernetes_service" "gateway" {
  metadata {
    name = "inference-gateway"
    annotations = {
      "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-type" = "nlb"
      "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-healthcheck-protocol" = "tcp"
      "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-healthcheck-port" = "traffic-port"
    }
  }
  spec {
    type = "NodePort"
    external_traffic_policy = "Local"
    port {
      name       = "tls"
      port       = 443
      target_port = 8080
    }
  }
}
```

kevin: also check gateway TLS listener config — sample: `spec.listeners[0].tls.certificateRefs[0].name = "inference-cert"` and Gateway must be in namespace `gateway-system` where `inference-cert` secret lives. if you need cross-namespace certs, we should update the controller RBAC, but that's a bigger change.

olga: noted. last thing — probes: can i keep http readiness on the pod and add a small tcp readiness sidecar just for NLB? or is that overkill?

jess: you can run two probes (kube supports only one readiness), but you can make the app respond on a small TCP health-port to satisfy NLB and have http readiness be part of the app's liveness. we did a tiny sidecar before (socat) to accept TCP and forward to http health endpoint. it's a bit hacky but works without changing app code.

olga: thanks all — i'll: create secret in gateway-system via cert-manager, update terraform svc annotations + externalTrafficPolicy, add tcp-friendly readiness (or sidecar), and open a PR. will ping when plan is up. :pray:

